          %title Lagrangians
          %h2#Lagrangians Lagrangians
          %p In this chapter we discuss the following topics:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#LagrangianDensities"} Lagrangian densities
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#ELFormsAndPresymplecticCurrents"} Euler-Lagrange forms and Presymplectic currents
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#ELEquationsOfMotion"} Euler-Lagrange equations of motion
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Given any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            (def.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FieldsAndFieldBundles"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+histories"} field histories
            that are to be regarded as “physically realizable” (if we think of the field theory as a description of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential equation
            – the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation+of+motion"} equation of motion
            – meaning that realizability of any field histories may be checked upon restricting the configuration to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhoods"} infinitesimal neighbourhoods
            (example
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinitesimalNeighbourhood"}
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field+theory"} local field theory
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JetBundleInTermsOfSyntheticDifferentialGeometry"}
            this means that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of a field theory are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations"} equations
            among the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
          %p
            For many field theories of interest, their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation+of+motion"} equation of motion
            is not a random
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+differential+equations"} partial differential equations
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+extremal+action"} principle of extremal action
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PrincipleOfExtremalAction"}
            below) determined by a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lagrangian+density"} local Lagrangian density
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalLagrangianDensityOnSecondOrderJetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            below). These are called
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theories"} Lagrangian field theories
          %p
            Namely among all the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+differential+forms"} variational differential forms
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VariationalBicomplexOnSecondOrderJetBundleOverTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi Σ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{0,0}_\Sigma(E)
            – the smooth functions – and the horizontal
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p+1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi Σ
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{p+1,0}_\Sigma(E)
            – to be called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+densities"} Lagrangian densities
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalLagrangianDensityOnSecondOrderJetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            below) – since these occupy the two “corners” of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+bicomplex"} variational bicomplex
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VariationalBicomplexDiagram"} (?)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+densities"} Lagrangian densities
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            do inherit special structure from their special position in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+bicomplex"} variational bicomplex
          %p
            Their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+derivative"} variational derivative
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \mathbf{L}
            uniquely decomposes as
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+derivative"} Euler-Lagrange derivative
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi EL
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_{EL} \mathbf{L}
                which is proportional to the variation of the fields (instead of their derivatives)
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+derivative"} total spacetime derivative
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi Θ
                        %mi BFV
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \Theta_{BFV}
                of a potential
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Θ
                        %mi BFV
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta_{BFV}
                for a
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+current"} presymplectic current
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi BFV
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi δ
                        %msub
                          %mi Θ
                          %mi BFV
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{BFV} \coloneqq \delta \Theta_{BFV}
          %p
            This is prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerLagrangeOperatorForTivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            below:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi EL
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mtext Euler-Lagrange variation
                  %mo −
                  %mi d
                  %munder
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Θ
                          %mi BFV
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mtext presymplectic current
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\delta \mathbf{L}
                  \\;=\;
                  \\underset{ \text{Euler-Lagrange variation}
                  }{\underbrace{\delta_{EL}\mathbf{L}}} - d \underset{\text{presymplectic current}}{\underbrace{\Theta_{BFV}}}
                  \\,.
          %p
            These two terms play a pivotal role in the theory: The condition that the first term vanishes on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+histories"} field histories
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential equation
            on field histories, called the
            %em
