              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+forms"} Euler-Lagrange forms
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+currents"} presymplectic currents
          %p
            The beauty of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalLagrangianDensityOnSecondOrderJetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            determines both the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of the fields as well as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+manifold"} presymplectic structure
            on the space of solutions to this equation (the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"}> shell
            ”), making it the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"}> covariant phase space
            ” of the theory. All this we discuss
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#PhaseSpace"} below
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+of+variational+differential+forms"} transgression of variational differential forms
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TransgressionOfVariationalDifferentialFormsToConfigrationSpaces"}
            below) of the following simple relation in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+bicomplex"} variational bicomplex
          #EulerLagrangeOperatorForTivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+form"} Euler-Lagrange form
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+current"} presymplectic current
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L} \in \Omega^{p+1,0}_\Sigma(E)
              as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalLagrangianDensityOnSecondOrderJetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi d
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d}\mathbf{L}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \mathbf{L}
              %em unique
              decomposition as a sum of two terms
            #eq:dLDecomposition.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (9)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi EL
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo −
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi Θ
                      %mi BFV
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{d} \mathbf{L}
                    \=
                    \\delta_{EL} \mathbf{L}
                    \-
                    d \Theta_{BFV}
            %p
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi EL
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_{EL}\mathbf{L}
              is proportional to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+derivative"} variational derivative
              of the fields (but not their derivatives, called a “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source+form"}> source form
              ”):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi EL
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi δ
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta_{EL} \mathbf{L}
                    \\;\in\;
                    \\Omega^{p+1,0}_{\Sigma}(E) \wedge \delta C^\infty(E)
                    \\;\subset\;
                    \\Omega^{p+1,1}_{\Sigma}(E)
                    \\,.
            %p The map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi EL
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi δ
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta_{EL} \;\colon\; \Omega^{p+1,0}_{\Sigma}(E) \longrightarrow \Omega^{p+1,0}_{\Sigma}(E) \wedge \delta \Omega^{0,0}_{\Sigma}(E)
            %p
              thus defined is called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+operator"} Euler-Lagrange operator
              and is explicitly given by the
              = succeed ":" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+derivative"} Euler-Lagrange derivative
            #eq:EulerLagrangeEquationGeneral.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (10)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi δ
                              %mi EL
                            %mi L
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi dvol
                              %mi Σ
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi δ
                                  %mi EL
                                %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %mi δ
                                %msup
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mi a
                            %mi δ
                            %msup
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi a
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi dvol
                              %mi Σ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %mi L
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %msup
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mi a
                              %mo −
                              %mfrac
                                %mi d
                                %mrow
                                  %mi d
                                  %msup
                                    %mi x
                                    %mi μ
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %mi L
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mi μ
                                    %mi a
                              %mo +
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi d
                                    %mn 2
                                %mrow
                                  %mi d
                                  %msup
                                    %mi x
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi μ
                                        %mn 1
                                  %mi d
                                  %msup
                                    %mi x
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi μ
                                        %mn 2
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %mi L
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi μ
                                        %mn 1
                                      %mo ,
                                      %msub
                                        %mi μ
                                        %mn 2
                                    %mi a
                              %mo −
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo )
                            %mi δ
                            %msup
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi a
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi dvol
                              %mi Σ
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\delta_{EL} L \, dvol_\Sigma
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \\frac{\delta_{EL} L}{\delta \phi^a}
                    \\delta \phi^a \wedge dvol_\Sigma
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\frac{\partial L}{\partial \phi^a}
                    \-
                    \\frac{d}{d x^\mu}
                    \\frac{\partial L}{\partial \phi^a_{,\mu}}
                    +
                    \\frac{d^2}{d x^{\mu_1} d x^{\mu_2}}
                    \\frac{\partial L}{\partial \phi^a_{\mu_1, \mu_2}}
                    \-
                    \\cdots
                    \\right)
                    \\delta \phi^a
                    \\wedge
                    dvol_\Sigma
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth subspace
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
              on which the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+form"} Euler-Lagrange form
              vanishes
            #eq:ShellInJetBundle.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (11)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi J
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi EL
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi ℰ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi J
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{E}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    x \in J^\infty_\Sigma(E)
                    \\;\vert\;
                    \\delta_{EL}\mathbf{L}(x) = 0
                    \\right\}
                    \\;\overset{i_{\mathcal{E}}}{\hookrightarrow}\;
                    J^\infty_\Sigma(E)
                    \\,.
            %p
              is called the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+spacetime+derivatives"} total spacetime derivatives
              vanish (the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+integrable+PDE"}> formally integrable prolongation
              ”) is the
              %em
                prolonged
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
            #eq:ProlongedShellInJetBundle.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (12)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi J
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi d
                              %mi k
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mn 1
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi k
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi EL
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mo )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo }
