                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{E}^\infty
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    x \in J^\infty_\Sigma(E)
                    \\;\vert\;
                    \\left(
                    \\frac{d^k}{d x^{\mu_1} \cdots d x^{\mu_k}}
                    \\delta_{EL}\mathbf{L}
                    \\right)(x) = 0
                    \\right\}
                    \\overset{i_{\mathcal{E}^\infty}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    J^\infty_\Sigma(E)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Saying something holds “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"}> on-shell
              ” is to mean that it holds after restriction to this subspace. For example a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+differential+form"} variational differential form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ,
                        %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in \Omega^{\bullet,\bullet}_\Sigma(E)
              is said to
              %em vanish on shell
              if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
