              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquationOfMotionOfDiracFieldIsDiracEquation"}
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PresymplecticCurrentDiracField"}
              below, and see remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupergeometricNatureOfDiracEquation"}
              below.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p#ELEquationsOfMotion
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
          %p
            The key implication of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+form"} Euler-Lagrange form
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            is that it induces the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation+of+motion"} equation of motion
            on the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+field+histories"} space of field histories
          #EulerLagrangeEquationsOnTrivialVectorFieldBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange
                = succeed ")" do
