              the corresponding
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+operator"} differential operator
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
              reads
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∂
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo +
                      %mi m
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    D
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left(
                    \- i \partial\!\!\!/\, + m
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field theory
              according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeFieldTheory"}
            %p
              Observe that the “square” of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+operator"} Klein-Gordon operator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo □
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mi m
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Box - m^2
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:KleinGordonEquation"} (29)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                              %mi i
                              %msup
                                %mi γ
                                %mi μ
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi μ
                              %mo +
                              %mi m
                              %mo )
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi i
                              %msup
                                %mi γ
                                %mi μ
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi μ
                              %mo +
                              %mi m
                              %mo )
                            %mi ψ
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi μ
                              %msup
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi μ
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi m
                                %mn 2
                              %mo )
                            %mi ψ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo □
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msup
                                %mi m
                                %mn 2
                              %mo )
                            %mi ψ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\left(
                    +i \gamma^\mu \partial_\mu + m
                    \\right)
                    \\left(-i \gamma^\mu \partial_\mu + m\right)\psi
                    \&amp;
                    \=
                    \\left(\partial_\mu \partial^\mu - m^2\right) \psi
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\left(\Box - m^2\right) \psi
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
              which solves the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+equations"} Dirac equations
              is in particular (on
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solution"} solution
              to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
          #SupergeometricNatureOfDiracEquation.num_prop
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometric
                nature of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+equation"} Dirac equation
                as an
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange equation
            %p
              While the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+equation"} Dirac equation
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DiracEquation"} (33)
              of example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquationOfMotionOfDiracFieldIsDiracEquation"}
              would make sense in itself also if the field coordinates
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
              and jet coordinates
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ,
                        %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_{,\mu}
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
              were not anti-commuting
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DiracFieldJetCoordinatesAnticommute"} (6)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometric
              nature (remark
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiracFieldSupergeometric"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LagrangianDensityOfDiracFieldSupergeometricNature"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange equation
              of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
          #DiracOperatorOnDiracSpinorsIsFormallySelfAdjointDifferentialOperator.num_example
            %h6#example_20 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+spinors"} Dirac spinors
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+self-adjoint+differential+operator"} formally self-adjoint differential operator
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"}> Dirac operator
                , hence the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+operator"} differential operator
                corresponding to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+equation"} Dirac equation
                of example
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquationOfMotionOfDiracFieldIsDiracEquation"}
                via def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialOperator"}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+self-adjoint+differential+operator"} formally anti-self adjoint
                (def.
                = succeed "):" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormallyAdjointDifferentialOperators"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    D^\ast = - D
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_10 Proof
            %p
              By
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DiracOperatorAsELOperator"} (32)
              we are to regard the Dirac operator as taking values in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+bundle"} dual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+bundle"} spin bundle
              by using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+conjugate"} Dirac conjugate
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{(-)}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DiracConjugate"} (?)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi Σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mo ×
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi Σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ψ
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ¯
                            %mi D
                            %mi Ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Gamma_\Sigma(\Sigma \times S)
                    \&amp;\overset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\Gamma_\Sigma(\Sigma \times S^\ast)
                    \\\
                    \\Psi &amp;\mapsto&amp; \overline{(-)} D \Psi
                    }
            %p
              Then we need to show that there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(-,-)
              such that for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor"} spinor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ψ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Ψ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi_1, \Psi_2
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mn 2
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi μ
                    %msub
                      %mi Ψ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi μ
                    %msub
                      %mi Ψ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\overline{\Psi_2}\gamma^\mu (\partial_\mu \Psi_1)
                    \-
                    \\overline{\Psi_1}\gamma^\mu (-\partial_\mu \Psi_2)
                    \\;=\;
                    d K(\psi_1, \psi_2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              But the spinor-to-vector pairing is symmetric
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SpinorToVectorPairingIsSymmetric"} (?)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi μ
                        %msub
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi μ
                    %msub
                      %mi Ψ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi μ
                    %msub
                      %mi Ψ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\overline{\partial_\mu \Psi_1}\gamma^\mu \Psi_2
                    +
                    \\overline{\Psi_1}\gamma^\mu (\partial_\mu \Psi_2)
                    \\;=\;
                    d K(\psi_1, \psi_2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+law"} product law
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiation
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi_1, \Psi_2
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Ψ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Ψ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Ψ
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ¯
                      %msup
                        %mi γ
                        %mi μ
                      %msub
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi μ
                    %mi dvol
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K(\Psi_1, \Psi_2)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left( \overline{\Psi_1} \gamma^\mu \Psi_2\right)
                    \\,
                    \\iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol
                    \\,.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            This concludes our discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+densities"} Lagrangian densities
            and their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational calculus
            %a{:href => "#Symmetries"} next chapter
            we consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetries+of+Lagrangians"} infinitesimal symmetries of Lagrangians
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+currents"} conserved currents
            that these induce via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noether%27s+theorem"} Noether's theorem
        .revisedby
